Still vulnerable in version 2.2.2:
- The whole attribute array, including the unsanitized `button.text`, is wr=
itten into `data-attributes` through `esc_attr( wp_json_encode() )`; `esc_a=
ttr` does not double-encode, so a value saved as `&amp;lt;svg&amp;gt;=E2=80=
=A6` (which gets past the kses filter WordPress applies to block attributes=
) reaches the browser's attribute parser as `&amp;lt;` and comes out as a r=
eal `&lt;svg&gt;` string after JSON.parse. build/render.php:70. Fix: Saniti=
ze `$attributes['button']['text']` with `wp_kses_post()` (applied to the de=
coded value) as is already done for `sliders[].title`/`desc`, or better, st=
op using `esc_attr` as the only defence for HTML-bearing values and sanitiz=
e every attribute that the frontend renders as HTML.
- The post-slide component sets `g =3D O(s, i, u?.text)`, which returns the=
 attacker's `button.text` unchanged when no ACF override is set, and passes=
 it to the anchor component as `dangerouslySetInnerHTML:{__html:g}`, so the=
 string is parsed as HTML and an `&lt;svg&gt;&lt;animate onbegin=3D=E2=80=
=A6&gt;` payload runs JavaScript as soon as the page loads. build/view.js:1=
. Fix: Render the button label as text (pass it as `children`) or run it th=
rough a sanitizer such as DOMPurify before using `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.

Attacker role: Contributor.
Impact: Stored XSS: JavaScript a Contributor saves in the block runs in the=
 browser of anyone who views the post, including administrators who preview=
 it, which allows session-riding actions such as creating admin accounts.

Hardening suggestions (not blockers):
- `O()`/`L()` in view.js also feeds ACF field values (`buttonText`, `title`=
) into `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, so any ACF value an author can edit is a =
second route to the same sink. build/view.js:1. Fix: Sanitize ACF-sourced v=
alues server-side in `Posts::arrangedPosts()` or on the client before inser=
ting them as HTML.
- In the `blocks` source type, the whole inner block content is base64-enco=
ded into `data-attributes-b64` and put back into the page with innerHTML, w=
ithout going through the core block render filters. build/render.php:11. Fi=
x: Run `$content` through `wp_kses_post()` (after the shortcodes are expand=
ed) before embedding it, unless the author has `unfiltered_html`.
